Summary:
Today’s session involved initiating the backend development phase for the Multi-Vendor E-commerce Platform. The focus was on setting up the project environment using Node.js and Express and organizing the basic folder structure. Initial work included establishing server configuration and preparing the connection setup for MongoDB. The foundation for handling different modules such as users, products, and orders was also outlined.

Outcomes:
A working backend setup was established with the server running successfully. The basic project structure was organized to support scalable development. Initial configurations for database connectivity and routing were prepared. This session created a strong base for implementing core backend functionalities in the upcoming days.
